Third-party material in scion-starlte (the Galaxy S9's device files for Scion)

Scion's kernel (github.com/Scion-Project/scion-kernel) is a fork of HakiOS by the HakiOS authors, and this repository is the S9's
device layer of that tree, which started as HakiOS's hakios-starlte. Its own files are under LICENSE (MIT). The kernel's NOTICE and
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md carry the full list; the parts that are in this repository:

- prebuilt/SILICIUM_UEFI.fd and prebuilt/BootShim.bin: built from Mu-Silicium (Project Silicium, Microsoft and contributors) with
  the port's changes, uefi/hakios.patch and uefi/files: BSD-2-Clause and BSD-2-Clause-Patent, the licences of the files they derive
  from. The UEFI image carries Project Silicium's Carbon Hypervisor (Hyp.bin, GPL-2.0, source at
  github.com/Project-Silicium/Carbon-Hypervisor). Recipe, base commit and hashes: prebuilt/README.md.
- prebuilt/mkbootimg.py: AOSP's, Apache-2.0.
- firmware/: the vendor's firmware binaries are NOT in this repository (since 7 Nov 2026; earlier commits held them). Only their sha256 sums
  are (firmware/*/SHA256SUMS), and tools/fetch-firmware.sh fetches them from the user's own copy or from the public LineageOS vendor
  trees pinned in it (github.com/ExyHyperBrick/proprietary_vendor_samsung_*, ExyHyperBrick's android_kernel_samsung_exynos9810 for the
  sensor hub): Samsung's and Broadcom's, redistribution terms "to verify" (the kernel's THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md). No Apple software,
  keys or Apple firmware is in this repository.
- Facts about the S9's hardware read from Samsung's published GPL kernel (LineageOS's android_kernel_samsung_exynos9810) and the
  LineageOS device and vendor trees: facts, not copied code.
